# Battle System Architecture

## Core Principles
- Focus on iterative development
- Maintain clear separation of battle phases
- Preserve real-time combat mechanics
- Ensure smooth animations and transitions

## Development Guidelines
CRITICAL: Maintain simplicity and focus in all battle system changes:
- Only implement what directly supports core gameplay
- Avoid complexity that doesn't serve gameplay goals
- Keep state management clear and centralized
- Maintain clear logging for debugging

### State Management Principles
- Maintain single source of truth for battalion states
- Avoid nested state updates
- Keep state transitions clear and traceable
- Use direct updates over complex callbacks

### Logging Standards
Logging must be precise and actionable:
- Always include the acting entity (battalion/node) ID
- Include state transitions and their reasons
- Group under consistent prefixes ([Battle], [Combat], [Target])
- Avoid redundant logs of the same event

Example log formats:
- Targeting: "[Battle] {battalionId} targeting {targetType} {targetId}"
- State Change: "[Battle] {nodeId} state changed from {oldState} to {newState}"
- Combat: "[Battle] {attackerId} dealing {damage} damage to {targetId}"
- Retargeting: "[Battle] {battalionId} retargeting from {oldTarget} - {reason}"

## Battle Flow

### 1. Pre-Battle Phase (3 seconds)
- Display countdown overlay
- Show deployment zones
- Animate network nodes and connection lines
- Initialize battalion health and positions

### 2. Active Battle Phase (20 seconds)
- Battle Timer
  - Simple 20-second countdown display
  - Located at screen top
  - No intermediate warnings
  - Continuous countdown until completion
- Maintain Active Combat
  - Show battalion stats (health/quantity)
  - Maintain animated network visualization
  - Continue all combat mechanics until timer end

### 3. Results Phase
- Results Overlay
  - Display immediately at timer end
  - Show final point totals for both parties
  - Indicate victor based on loss calculations
  - Display tiebreaker results if applicable

### Combat Mechanics

#### Battalion Behavior
- Movement
  - Speed scaled by battalion speed stat
  - Follow network connection lines
  - Stop at attack range from target
  - Smooth animation transitions

- Combat
  - Attack power based on type and quantity
  - Health scaled by type and quantity
  - Damage triggers visual feedback
  - Destroyed battalions removed from field

#### Targeting System
- Initial Target Selection
  - Primary: Always target neutral nodes first
  - Secondary: Enemy battalions (if no neutral nodes)
  - Guardians only target nodes
  - Target closest valid option in range

- Retargeting Logic (Simplified)
  - Only retarget when:
    1. Current target is destroyed
    2. Node is captured (no longer neutral)
  - No retargeting for distance optimization
  - Immediate movement to new target when needed

#### Node Control
- Node Health: 75% of total battalion health combined
- Control States
  - Enemy (Red)
  - Neutral (Purple)
  - User (Blue)
- Progress visualization during capture
- Affects battalion pathfinding

#### Node Capture Mechanics
- Multi-Battalion Capture System
  - Each battalion's damage contributes to their party's capture progress
  - Multiple battalions can attack simultaneously
  - Each attack must trigger distinct animations and damage calculations
  - Final capture credited to attacking party (user/enemy), not individual battalion
  - Track and calculate opposing forces (user vs enemy battalions) separately

#### Combat Visualization
- Battalion Identification
  - Visual type indicators (B: Breacher, G: Guardian, P: Phreak)
  - Unique battalion IDs for tracking and logging
  - Clear party affiliation (user/enemy) indicators
- Attack Sequence
  - Individual attack animations for each battalion
  - Corresponding damage response from target
  - Visual distinction between user and enemy attacks
  - Clear capture progress indication

### Visual Feedback System
#### Node Feedback
- Health Visualization
  - Clear health bar display
  - Capture progress indicator
  - Color-coded control state (Red/Purple/Blue)
  - Smooth health transitions
- Combat Effects
  - Receive damage flash animation
  - Capture progress visual feedback
  - Party-based capture indication
  - Clear visual state transitions

#### Battalion Feedback
- Health System
  - Total health = Bot type base health × quantity
  - Health bar reflects current state
  - Visual quantity indicator
  - Clear damage state representation
- Combat Animations
  - Attack initiation flash
  - Target damage response flash
  - Movement during targeting/retargeting
  - Range indication at attack position

#### Combat Range Visualization
- Attack Range
  - Visual indication of attack range
  - Clear stop position at range edge
  - Battalion-to-target connection indicator
  - Range-based positioning feedback

#### Attack Sequence Flow
1. Movement Phase
   - Clear path visualization
   - Smooth movement to range edge
   - Stop at attack range
   - Position stabilization

2. Attack Phase
   - Attacker animation flash
   - Target response animation
   - Health/state updates
   - Multiple battalion coordination

3. State Updates
   - Health bar updates
   - Capture progress updates
   - Battalion state changes
   - Visual state synchronization

#### Combat Tracking
- Attack Registration
  - Log each battalion's attacks separately
  - Track damage contribution by party
  - Monitor simultaneous attacks from multiple sources
  - Maintain clear attack order and timing
- State Management
  - Track current node control progress
  - Monitor attacking battalions and their parties
  - Record damage contributions by party
  - Update control state based on cumulative party damage

### 4. Victory Conditions
#### Scoring System
- Mark-Based Point Values
  - Mark 1: 1 point per bot
  - Mark 2: 2 points per bot
  - Mark 3: 4 points per bot
  - Mark 4: 8 points per bot
- Point Calculation
  - Track losses per battalion
  - Sum total points based on mark values
  - Bot type does not affect point value
  - Lower total = better performance

#### Victory Determination
- Primary Victory Condition
  - Party with lowest total loss points wins
  - Track running point totals during battle
  - Update loss calculations in real-time
- Tiebreaker Rule
  - In case of equal point losses
  - Defending party retains one bot
  - Defending party declared victor

#### Loss Tracking
- Battalion Loss Monitoring
  - Track quantity changes per battalion
  - Calculate point value based on mark
  - Maintain running total per party
  - Log all loss events

### Node Strategic Effects
#### Network Multiplier System
- Node Control Benefits
  - Applies multiplier to connected lines
  - Affects both incoming/outgoing connections
  - Controlled by capturing party
- Battalion Stat Boosts
  - Small stat increase when:
    1. Attacking from controlled line
    2. Defending on controlled line
  - Applies to controlling party's battalions only
- Future Strategic Value
  - Not tied to victory conditions
  - Provides tactical advantage
  - Influences battle positioning
  - Affects combat effectiveness

