## Technical Requirements
- Efficient pathfinding along network
- Smooth animation transitions
  - Use native driver for animations where possible
  - Maintain 60fps performance target
  - Implement proper cleanup on unmount
- Real-time combat calculations
  - Follow platform-agnostic state patterns
  - Maintain direct, predictable updates
  - Avoid nested state mutations
- Responsive retargeting system
- Accurate health/damage tracking
- Synchronized visual feedback

## Movement System
### Network-Based Movement
- Pathfinding Priority
  1. Follow network connection lines between nodes
  2. Calculate optimal path to target using network topology
  3. Fallback to direct path if performance impact is too high
  - Performance monitoring to ensure smooth gameplay

### Movement Animation
- Visual Requirements
  - Smooth transitions along network paths
  - Clear indication of battalion movement state
  - Consistent animation speed based on battalion type
  - Proper cleanup of animation resources

### Movement Synchronization
- State Coordination
  - Sync movement state with combat actions
  - Coordinate multiple battalion movements
  - Handle interrupted movements (retargeting)
  - Maintain performance during mass movement

### Performance Thresholds
- Movement Optimization
  - Monitor frame rate during pathfinding
  - Track animation performance metrics
  - Implement fallback strategies if needed
  - Balance visual quality with performance

## Performance Guidelines
1. Animation Optimization
   - Prefer native-driven animations
   - Batch animation updates
   - Minimize JS bridge traffic
   - Clean up animations properly

2. State Management
   - Use platform-agnostic patterns
   - Maintain direct state updates
   - Follow unified data flow
   - Keep state transitions atomic

3. Error Handling
   - Follow backend error standards
   - Maintain clear error boundaries
   - Log errors consistently
   - Recover gracefully from failures

Remember: Any change that doesn't directly support these core mechanics should be carefully evaluated before implementation.